            <ArticleTitle>Lymphangioma of the clivus: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E779; discussion E779</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Different clival lesions have been reported in the literature previously. The lymphangioma reported in the present case seems to be the first lesion localized in the clivus.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CLINICAL PRESENTATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">The patient presented with a history of diplopia and headache. Imaging studies showed a lytic lesion at the cranial base.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Transsphenoidal excision of the lesion resulted in total resolution of the patient's complaints.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Lymphangioma must be kept in mind for the differential diagnosis of lytic lesions of the cranial base. Surgical removal leads to immediate improvement of the symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
